    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I reproduced this on latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nI have the following colorscheme setup in MiniMax\n\n```\nMiniDeps.now(function()\n  add(\"rose-pine/neovim\")\n\n  require(\"rose-pine\").setup({\n    styles = {\n      transparency = true,\n    },\n  })\n  vim.cmd(\"color rose-pine\")\nend)\n```\n\nThe `transparency` setting works in normal terminal, but not in tmux. I also have other distros (LazyVim, AstroNvim) setup and they don't have this particular problem.\n\nI'm on Mac 26.1 (25B78) with the following `nvim` and `tmux` versions.\n\n```\nNVIM v0.11.5\nBuild type: Release\nLuaJIT 2.1.1761727121\n\ntmux 3.6a\n```\n\nLet me know if you need anything else. It's an odd one and quite possible because there is something weird with my setup, but thought I should report here for your information.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n- Install MiniMax\n- Setup `rose-pine` (or `tokyonight` theme)\n- Launch nvim in `tmux`",
